+**Mini-charter — REQUIRED right after the kickoff beat (cost tracking, CONTRACTS §10.3).** Two
+twins, machine then human:
+
+1. **Issue-body marker.** Append one line to the issue body (same `--body-file -` edit idiom as
+   the `<!-- discord-thread: <id> -->` marker; use `hooks/gh-issue.sh`):
+
+   `<!-- falcon:charter:v1 {"v":1,"issue":"<owner>/<repo>#<n>","kickoff_at":"<now iso8601>","planned":[…],"charter_variant":"<from token-usage.sh's variant — or vendor VARIANT@pin>"} -->`
+
+   `planned` lists the crew you expect to dispatch for this issue class — agent, role, and model
+   read from `vendor/falcon-dev-common/config/team-roster.yaml` (planned ≠ actual: workers'
+   `falcon:usage:v1` reports carry the actual model, and Step 6b flags mismatches in the ledger).
+   Typical pipeline plan: yoda → obi-wan → builder (whichever you'll load-balance to) → chewie,
+   plus ackbar when the repo profile deploys. `priority:asap` skips make the plan shorter — list
+   what you will actually dispatch.
+
+2. **🧭 Team-plan card** in the issue's Discord thread, Format Standard:
+
+   ```
+   🧭 **Team plan — <repo>#<n>**
+   • Scope: <one line — this issue only, or the issue set>
+   • Crew: Yoda (triage) → Obi-wan (architecture) → Han (build) → Chewie (review) — all on sonnet
+   • 💸 Cost tracking on (variant: <full|lite>)
+   ```
+
+Both are non-blocking on failure (log + proceed to dispatch), but a missing charter marker means
+Step 6b's ledger row will carry `planned: null` — log loudly. Never edit an existing
+`falcon:charter:v1` marker; if the crew changes mid-issue (kickback to a different builder), the
+actuals in the usage reports are the record.
+
 **Do NOT send a Telegram DM for this kickoff** — it is an in-flight coordination beat. Matt will see it in the issue's Discord thread. Do **not** block dispatch on a Discord post failure; log it and proceed.
 
